{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"In general, to find the derivative (i.e. the expression for $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ ) of a function defined parametrically by the equations $x=u(t)$ and $y=v(t)$ (where $u$ and $v$ are any functions of $t$), we use the following rule:\n\n$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{dy}{dt}\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{dx}{dt}\\right)}=\\dfrac{v'(t)}{u'(t)}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"We are given that $x=\\ln(1-2t)$ and $y=\\dfrac{1}{3t}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\u0026=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{d}{dt}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{3t}\\right)}{\\dfrac{d}{dt}(\\ln(1-2t))}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{-\\dfrac{1}{3t^2}}{-\\dfrac{2}{1-2t}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1-2t}{6t^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{Simplify}}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{1-2t}{6t^2}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"A curve in the plane is defined parametrically by the equations $x=\\ln(1-2t)$ and $y=\\dfrac{1}{3t}$.\n\n**Find $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{1-2t}{6t^2}$","correct":true},{"content":"$-\\dfrac{1}{3t^2}$","correct":false},{"content":"$-\\dfrac{2}{\\ln(1-2t)}$","isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{1-2t}{9t^2}$","isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
